# Translations

Spotlight uses gettext for internationalization. The gettext domain is `spotlight`.

## Structure

Source translation files (`.po`) are placed in this directory as `<lang>.po` (e.g., `fr.po`, `es.po`).

At build and install time, these are compiled to binary `.mo` files and placed at:
```
locale/<lang>/LC_MESSAGES/spotlight.mo
```

This matches the structure used by GNOME extensions in the wild, where compiled
translation files ship inside the installed extension.

## Adding a New Translation

1. Copy the template to start a new language:
   ```bash
   msginit -i locale/spotlight.pot -o locale/fr.po -l fr
   ```

2. Edit `locale/fr.po` with translated strings using a PO editor or text editor.

3. The build script automatically compiles all `.po` files to `.mo` during install.

## Updating the Template

To regenerate the translation template from source strings:
```bash
xgettext --from-code=UTF-8 \
    --copyright-holder="Spotlight contributors" \
    --package-name="Spotlight" \
    --package-version="2026.08.25" \
    --output=locale/spotlight.pot \
    *.js prefs/*.js
```

## Installed Layout

When installed, translations appear at:
```
~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/spotlight@nin/
    locale/
        fr/LC_MESSAGES/spotlight.mo
        es/LC_MESSAGES/spotlight.mo
        ...
```
